WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.160
It's normal to worry about the legal side of helping, but good Samaritan laws are generally

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:09.800
there to protect you as long as you act in good faith.

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:14.280
These laws exist in every state to support people who step up, though the specific details

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:19.040
can vary, so it's always a good idea to be familiar with your local rules.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:22.600
Always prioritize your own safety and skills when deciding to act.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:27.480
If you do choose to assist, you must stay with the person until professional help arrives.

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:32.680
While providing care, please protect their privacy by sharing information only with EMS

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:36.279
and keeping personal details or photos off of social media.

00:00:36.279 --> 00:00:38.599
Stick to the skills you are trained for today.

00:00:38.599 --> 00:00:42.759
If you are asked to do something beyond your certification, politely decline and wait for

00:00:42.759 --> 00:00:44.119
the pros.

00:00:44.119 --> 00:00:47.520
Always ask an alert person for verbal consent before you start.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:51.720
If a conscious person refuses your help, you must respect that choice, though you should

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:56.520
still call 911 if it is a life-threatening emergency and document the refusal.

